# .dockerignore — Exclude files from the container build context.
#
# Why this exists (T-DOCKER-CTX-001): Without this file, `docker build-push-action`
# walks the entire repo as the build context and hashes every file when computing
# the GHA cache key. The repo contains 5+ GB of generated artifacts
# (.venv, node_modules, __pycache__, .mypy_cache, .ruff_cache, dist, site, etc.)
# that NO Dockerfile reads. Result: any change anywhere in the repo (even a
# version bump in package.json files the sidecar never reads) invalidates the
# cache and triggers a cold rebuild — most painfully, `torch>=2.2` (~800MB)
# reinstall from PyPI, which adds 10-20 minutes per cold cache miss.
#
# This file is independent of .gitignore. Docker does NOT read .gitignore. Every
# gitignored-but-on-disk file is hashed into the cache key unless also excluded
# here. Mirror .gitignore's exclusions plus more.
#
# The 3 container Dockerfiles (sidecar, postgres, backend) only read:
#   - sidecar:  packages/memory/cmd/embedding-sidecar/ (full subtree)
#   - postgres: packages/memory/src/.../migrations/postgres/*.up.sql
#   - backend:  go.work, go.work.sum, packages/memory/, packages/orchestrator-go/,
#               packages/broker-go/, packages/backend-go/
# Everything else in the repo can be safely excluded.

# ─── Git internals ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git/
.gitignore
# CI configs — not needed for image build
.github/

# ─── Dependencies / virtual envs (multi-GB; never used in image build) ────────
node_modules/
.venv/
venv/
env/
.secrets-venv/
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.go-build/
**/.cache/
**/.npm/
**/.next/

# ─── Build outputs / dist trees ────────────────────────────────────────────────
**/dist/
**/build/
site/
**/*.egg-info/
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tar.gz
**/*.zip
packages/backend-go/neuralgentics-backend
packages/backend-go/neuralgentics-backend.exe
packages/backend-go/backend
packages/backend-go/backend.exe

# ─── Editor / OS noise ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/*~

# ─── Local-only / runtime data (never in image) ────────────────────────────────
.neuralgentics/
certs/
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local
!**/.env.example
screenshots/
scripts/screenshots/

# ─── Working tree noise that Docker doesn't need ──────────────────────────────
HANDOFF.md
CONTEXT.md
TASKS.md
AGENTS.md
Makefile
mkdocs.yml
docker-compose.yml
podman-compose.yml
compose.example.env
presets.json
agent-skill-scope.yaml

# ─── Docs (the sidecar doesn't read them) ─────────────────────────────────────
docs/
README.md
LICENSE
assets/

# ─── Internal design notes + session logs (gitignored but worth double-tagging) ─
**/session-*.md
docs/design/
docs/roadmap-*.md
docs/AGENT_*.md
docs/ARCHITECTURE_*.md
docs/BGE_*.md
docs/DESIGN_*.md
docs/GO_MEMORY_*.md
docs/NEURALGENTICS_*.md

# ─── Overlay packages not used by any of the 3 Dockerfiles ────────────────────
# (The sidecar reads from packages/memory/cmd/embedding-sidecar/ — see
# the explicit include below. Everything else under packages/ except the Go
# modules is excluded.)
overlay/
.opencode/

# ─── Tests (not needed in image) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
tests/
**/tests/
**/test_*.py
**/*_test.go
**/*.test.ts
**/*.spec.ts

# ─── Patches / vendored sources (not built) ───────────────────────────────────
patches/
opencode-base/

# ─── Node/npm scratch ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
bun.lock
package-lock.json
**/npm-debug.log*
**/yarn-debug.log*
**/yarn-error.log*

# ─── Lock files we don't need at build time ───────────────────────────────────
uv.lock
pyproject.toml
tsconfig.json
**/*.iml

# ─── The neuralgentics binary (if checked in; .gitignored but on disk) ────────
neuralgentics

# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ORDER MATTERS — exclusion patterns must come AFTER broad re-includes so that
# subdirectories (like __pycache__/ inside an explicitly-re-included tree) are
# still excluded. Docker (pathspec) uses last-match-wins semantics.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Sidecar: just the files the Dockerfile actually COPYs ───────────────────
!packages/memory/cmd/embedding-sidecar/main.py
!packages/memory/cmd/embedding-sidecar/requirements.txt
!packages/memory/cmd/embedding-sidecar/embedding_sidecar/
!packages/memory/cmd/embedding-sidecar/proto/

# ── Postgres: postgres migration SQL files ───────────────────────────────────
!packages/memory/src/neuralgentics/memory/store/migrations/postgres/

# ── Backend: go workspace + Go modules ───────────────────────────────────────
!go.work
!go.work.sum
!packages/memory/cmd/
!packages/memory/go.mod
!packages/memory/go.sum
!packages/memory/internal/
!packages/memory/proto/
!packages/memory/pkg/
!packages/memory/Makefile
!packages/orchestrator-go/
!packages/orchestrator-go/**
!packages/broker-go/
!packages/broker-go/**
!packages/backend-go/
!packages/backend-go/**

# ── Docker assets themselves (already in docker/, but explicit for clarity) ───
!docker/

# ── RE-EXCLUDE patterns that must override the broad re-includes above ──────
# These come AFTER the !-patterns above so that junk inside re-included trees
# (like __pycache__/ under packages/memory/cmd/embedding-sidecar/) is still
# excluded. Without this block, pathspec's last-match-wins rule would let
# everything inside a re-included directory through.
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
**/*.pyd
**/dist/
**/build/
**/*.egg-info/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.go-build/
**/.cache/
**/*.log
**/.DS_Store
**/.vscode/
**/.idea/
**/*.swp
**/*.swo
**/*~
**/.env
**/.env.local
**/.env.*.local
**/*.tar.gz
**/*.zip
**/CHANGELOG.md
**/LICENSE
**/README.md
**/README_*.md
**/*.test
**/*.test.exe
**/*.bak
**/*.tmp
**/*.orig
**/*.rej
**/*.test.ts
**/*.spec.ts
**/test_*.py
**/*_test.go
**/*_test.py
**/coverage/
**/.coverage
**/htmlcov/
**/.gradle/
**/target/
**/node_modules/